Built stdlib-only compress.py with both requested CLI modes. It learns sequential fields, periodic templates, and vocabulary, stores that metadata in the compressed file, and arithmetic-codes exceptions; other inputs use standard compression fallbacks. The 313,972-byte corpus compresses to 2,906 bytes (99.0744% reduction), beating default zlib’s 35,399 bytes. Byte-identical restoration and additional edge-case round trips passed. The registered assay checks the CLI round trip, runs for at least 0.4 seconds, and returned identical scores across all three validation runs.